summary:
- topic: Special Meeting Purpose
  text: The special meeting was convened to approve the FY26 budget articles, a function
    typically performed at the May meeting, but expedited due to the City Council's
    scheduling of their budget vote.
- topic: Superintendent's Report
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina provided an overview of the budget calendar,
    announced three resignations (Erica Matio, Samantha Matoya, LB Murphy), and promoted
    a community food drive.
- topic: FY26 Budget Article Reading
  text: The Superintendent read aloud 19 detailed budget articles, outlining expenditures
    for various cost centers including regular instruction, special education, and
    facilities, as well as local contributions and capital improvement plans.
- topic: Budget Article 3.1 Vote
  text: Budget Article 3.1, concerning regular instruction expenditures, was voted
    on separately. Board Chair Rosemarie DeAngelis voted against it, citing concerns
    about social-emotional learning funds, but the motion passed 4-2.
- topic: Grouped Budget Article Votes
  text: The remaining budget articles were grouped into two motions (3.2-3.11 and
    3.12-3.19) and passed unanimously by the board, streamlining the approval process.
- topic: Local Funding Justification
  text: The board justified exceeding the state's EPS funding model by over $17 million,
    citing reasons such as co-curricular costs, nursing services, maintaining four
    elementary schools, and lower class size targets.
- topic: Board Comments and Adjournment
  text: Board members reflected on the challenging budget process, expressing appreciation
    for the administration's work and acknowledging differences of opinion as representative
    of the community. The meeting was then adjourned.
